  "fixture_kind": "public_exact-list_card_data",
  "rulings": [
    {
      "comment": "If you Donate an Aura, it stays where it is, but the targeted player now controls it.",
      "oracle_id": "049d1fb2-cce7-40e7-a633-e84cf9782d89",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Gideon's first ability causes him to become a creature with the creature types Human, Soldier, and Ally. He remains a planeswalker with the planeswalker type Gideon. (He also retains any other card types or subtypes he may have had.) Each subtype is correlated to the proper card type: planeswalker is only a type (not a creature type), and Human, Soldier, and Ally are just creature types (not planeswalker types).",
      "oracle_id": "51eae7ff-fed9-4afe-8053-7690379449dd",
      "published_at": "2015-08-25",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Gideon's first ability doesn't count as a creature entering the battlefield. Gideon was already on the battlefield; he only changed his types. Specifically, your rally abilities won't trigger. (Of course, Gideon's second ability will cause rally abilities to trigger.)",
      "oracle_id": "51eae7ff-fed9-4afe-8053-7690379449dd",
      "published_at": "2015-08-25",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If Gideon becomes a creature the same turn he enters the battlefield, you can't attack with him or use any of his {T} abilities (if he gains any).",
      "oracle_id": "51eae7ff-fed9-4afe-8053-7690379449dd",
      "published_at": "2015-08-25",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If damage that can't be prevented is dealt to Gideon after his first ability has resolved, that damage will have all applicable results: specifically, the damage is marked on Gideon (since he's a creature) and that damage causes that many loyalty counters to be removed from him (since he's a planeswalker). Even though he has indestructible, if Gideon has no loyalty counters on him, he's put into his owner's graveyard.",
      "oracle_id": "51eae7ff-fed9-4afe-8053-7690379449dd",
      "published_at": "2015-08-25",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If Sorin leaves the battlefield after you've activated his first loyalty ability during your turn but before it resolves, you'll still gain 1 life as that ability deals damage.",
      "oracle_id": "cffb615c-2de0-4c65-9d0b-08a649ba0695",
      "published_at": "2019-05-03",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a card in a graveyard has {X} in its mana cost, X is considered to be 0.",
      "oracle_id": "cffb615c-2de0-4c65-9d0b-08a649ba0695",
      "published_at": "2019-05-03",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Multiple instances of lifelink on the same creature or planeswalker are redundant.",
      "oracle_id": "cffb615c-2de0-4c65-9d0b-08a649ba0695",
      "published_at": "2019-05-03",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Emblems behave similarly to enchantments: They have an ability that, in a general sense, continually affects the game. The primary difference between them is that emblems aren\u2019t permanents and don\u2019t exist on the battlefield. Nothing in the game can remove an emblem, simply because no other spell or ability references them. Once you get an emblem, you keep it for the rest of the game. Emblems have no color, name, card type, or other characteristics beyond the listed ability.",
      "oracle_id": "eab0d8b9-c66f-402f-b259-f46f15cefd78",
      "published_at": "2011-01-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Lethal damage and effects that say \u201cdestroy\u201d won\u2019t cause a permanent with indestructible to be put into the graveyard. However, a permanent with indestructible can be put into the graveyard for a number of reasons. The most likely reasons are if it\u2019s sacrificed, if it\u2019s a creature whose toughness is 0 or less, or if it\u2019s an Aura that\u2019s either unattached or attached to something illegal.",
      "oracle_id": "eab0d8b9-c66f-402f-b259-f46f15cefd78",
      "published_at": "2013-07-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An opponent\u2019s spell that targets a single creature or enchantment you control more than once costs only {1} more to cast. An opponent\u2019s spell that targets multiple creatures and/or enchantments you control costs {1} more for each of them.",
      "oracle_id": "faf081dc-1fb2-47ac-a9c7-8001b4904120",
      "published_at": "2020-01-24",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Callaphe\u2019s last ability applies to itself as well as other creatures and enchantments you control.",
      "oracle_id": "faf081dc-1fb2-47ac-a9c7-8001b4904120",
      "published_at": "2020-01-24",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Callaphe\u2019s last ability gives only one instance of the ability to creatures you control that are also enchantments.",
      "oracle_id": "faf081dc-1fb2-47ac-a9c7-8001b4904120",
      "published_at": "2020-01-24",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Colorless and generic mana symbols ({C}, {0}, {1}, {2}, {X}, and so on) in mana costs of permanents you control don\u2019t count toward your devotion to any color.",
      "oracle_id": "faf081dc-1fb2-47ac-a9c7-8001b4904120",
      "published_at": "2020-01-24",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Hybrid mana symbols, monocolored hybrid mana symbols, and Phyrexian mana symbols do count toward your devotion to their color(s).",
      "oracle_id": "faf081dc-1fb2-47ac-a9c7-8001b4904120",
      "published_at": "2020-01-24",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If an activated ability or triggered ability has an effect that depends on your devotion to a color, you count the number of mana symbols of that color among the mana costs of permanents you control as the ability resolves. The permanent with that ability will be counted if it\u2019s still on the battlefield at that time.",
      "oracle_id": "faf081dc-1fb2-47ac-a9c7-8001b4904120",
      "published_at": "2020-01-24",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If you put an Aura on an opponent\u2019s permanent, you still control the Aura, and mana symbols in its mana cost count towards your devotion.",
      "oracle_id": "faf081dc-1fb2-47ac-a9c7-8001b4904120",
      "published_at": "2020-01-24",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Mana symbols in the text boxes of permanents you control don\u2019t count toward your devotion to any color.",
      "oracle_id": "faf081dc-1fb2-47ac-a9c7-8001b4904120",
      "published_at": "2020-01-24",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The ability that defines Callaphe\u2019s power works in all zones, not just the battlefield.",
      "oracle_id": "faf081dc-1fb2-47ac-a9c7-8001b4904120",
      "published_at": "2020-01-24",
      "source": "wotc"
    }
  ],
